-*- mode: org -*-
* Guix Daemon (gxd)

A Guile implementation of a build daemon for Guix.

** Namespace

The name =gxd= is choosen as a namespace for the next Guix Daemon (aiming to be included to Guix v2.0) because it is:
- short
- ending on =d= as in ~sshd~, ~mpd~, etc.
- few name colisions in Guix/Linux namespaces
- 'rhymes' with the (legacy) C++ daemon =nix=
- sounds native :)

** Repository Structure

First level directories are the standard:
- src
- tests
- env
- dev

Second level directory is =gxd=. It used as a name-space for guile modules to avoid name collisions.

In general try to keep directory structure simple and add more nesting as needed following principles described in [[https://trop.in/blog/a-sane-directory-structure-for-software-projects][A Sane Directory Structure for Software Project]] blog post by Andrew Tropin.

** Development

Workflow fo interactive Guile development

Start the Guile nREPL server:

#+BEGIN_SRC bash
  make ares
#+END_SRC

If you edit .scm files in Emacs run =M-x arei= to connect current buffer to nREPL server.

*** Dev Sandboxes

Sandboxed to test guix-daemon in is created by ~guix shell --container~

The sandbox filesystem:
- =/tmp=, =/dev=, =/proc=, and =/sys= are created by ~guix shell --container~
- =/gnu/store= is bind mounted by ~guix shell --container~
  - by default it mounts to the host =/gnu/store= as read-only
  - if =/gnu/store= is explicitly mounded to another dir, e.g. ~--share=/gnu/store=/tmp/fake-gnu-store~, the packages provided to the ~guix shell --container~ as well as their requisites (e.g, ~guix gc --requisites coreutils~) are hard linked from the host =/gnu/store=
- needs to be created/mounted in the container by hand (for substitutes to work)
  - =/var/log/guix/acl= (Public-Key Infrastructure (SPKI) Access-Control Lists)
- automatically populated by ~guix-daemon~?
  - =/var/guix/daemon-socket/socket=
  - =/var/guix/gc.lock=
  - =/var/guix/gcroots=
  - =/var/guix/temproots=
  - =/var/log/guix=
  - =/etc/guix=
  - =touch ./var/guix/db/db.sqlite=

Caveats:
- =guix-daemon= and client commands are run from the same unprivileged user inside sandbox
- unprivileged user inside sandbox is stripped from namespace capabilities (no isolated builds)
- by defaul =guix= inside the container is pinned to v1.5 (need to package current version)

